# The site's own settings are never committed.
#
# SETTINGS.default is the shipped configuration and IS tracked; SETTINGS is the
# copy a site edits. Committing one means the next tarball drop overwrites the
# settings of whatever cluster it is unpacked on with another cluster's -- a
# node list, a drain switch and a job set, all replaced silently by an upgrade.
SETTINGS

# Per-node output, written on the cluster.
results/
logs/
reports/*.csv
